35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It seems we often strive for the grand and the universal, yet it is the small, focused tools that truly endure in the hearts of the workers.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... the budget is... it's a bit strange. The capital budget is frozen, but there's some room in the software allowance. But the licences... they get more expensive as we grow.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Sakura,,Oh no! I found something super weird! Some of the customer plants have no signal at all! And the developers are way too busy to help us right now!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The data is clear. We are losing hours every single day to redundant data entry and simple address errors. These are the ""invisible"" losses we ignore.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Sakura, you are correct about the developers. Furthermore, the coordination group is severely understaffed. We are relying on a few people to do everything manually.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Ryuji, your findings on wasted time are a call to action. If we can solve a specific pain, we create a lasting value.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,If we pick a project that uses per-head licences... we might not be able to afford the renewal next year. I'm... I'm really worried about that.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, don't be sad! Maybe we can find a project that doesn't need fancy licences! But we definitely can't do anything that needs a lot of coding!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Exactly. We should avoid any proposal that requires heavy developer involvement or expensive scaling. We need a solution for the floor, not a fancy software suite.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. Any proposal that assumes ""coordination"" happens automatically is a fantasy. We must choose a project that reduces the manual burden on the existing staff.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,It is a beautiful realization. We must seek a project that is modest in scope but deep in impact. A small seed that grows into a sturdy tree.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I agree. A fixed-fee project would be safer. It wouldn't leave us with a surprise bill later.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Sakura,,I just hope the project doesn't need us to go to those plants with no signal! That would be like trying to call a ghost!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,We must prioritize the elimination of redundant record-copying. That is a tangible loss of productivity that affects everyone every day.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, that is the most logical path. If we reduce the manual data entry, we alleviate the pressure on the understaffed coordination group without needing new hires.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
