60,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Looking at these, Proposal A seems the most aligned with the lessons of the past. It is a focused tool for a specific, recurring pain.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,Proposal A... it sounds like it might be a fixed-fee setup for the catalog. It doesn't seem like it would have those scary per-user licence costs.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Sakura,,I don't like Proposal D! I told you the signal is bad at the plants! The app would just spin and spin and then everyone would be grumpy!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Proposal A directly addresses the misrouted deliveries and the time lost to copying records. It solves the actual problem on the floor.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Proposal B sounds like it would just create more ""coordination"" work for the people already struggling. Proposal A is the only one that reduces the actual workload.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, your insight is keen. We must not mistake ""automation of reporting"" for ""reduction of work."" Proposal A removes the root cause.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I feel a bit more confident about A. It seems the safest for the budget and the most helpful for the people.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Sakura,,Yay! A is like a big treasure map where everyone knows where the gold is! No more guessing!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,It is the only rational choice. It targets the systemic inefficiency of fragmented data without requiring a massive developer overhaul or expensive infrastructure.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"It is the only option that respects the current staffing limits. By standardizing the records, we stop the bleeding of time and effort.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,"It is rare to find such harmony in a room. We have looked at the past, the present, and the constraints, and they all point to one path.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'm glad we talked about the budget... I think I can support A without worrying too much now.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Sakura,,I'm just happy we aren't doing the app! Imagine the faces of the technicians when the app crashes in a basement! Teehee!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,The evidence is overwhelming. The cost of inaction on the data fragmentation is higher than the cost of implementing Proposal A.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,Logic dictates that Proposal A is the most sustainable choice. It provides the highest utility with the lowest risk to our human resources.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
